# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit .env.
# Accounts on QRL Zond are ML-DSA-87; there is no secp256k1 private key.
DEPLOYER_MNEMONIC="<34-word QRL mnemonic>"

# Written by `npm run gen:deployer` so kurtosis-up.sh can fund it at genesis
# without reading the seed. On testnet v3 (QIP-55) this is the 64-byte form,
# Q + 128 hex; its first 40 hex equal the address the same mnemonic had on
# the 20-byte line, so re-running gen:deployer after `npm install` extends it
# in place. kurtosis-up.sh refuses a 40-hex value under the v3 image set.
DEPLOYER_ADDRESS="<Q + 128 hex, from gen:deployer>"

# Private network only. scripts/qrl.js refuses any non-local host unless
# ALLOW_PUBLIC_RPC=1, so that iterating never litters the shared public testnet.
# Point QRL_RPC_URL at the Kurtosis enclave's mapped EL port; kurtosis-up.sh
# writes it here for you. The enclave's chain id is 3151908 - 1337 is the PUBLIC
# QRL testnet, which is exactly what this repo refuses to deploy to.
QRL_RPC_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8545"
QRL_CHAIN_ID=3151908

# Escape hatch for a deliberate public deployment. Leave unset.
# ALLOW_PUBLIC_RPC=1

# Where the genesis puts the beacon deposit contract. Defaults to the v2
# 20-byte form (0x + '42' x 20); the v3 / QIP-55 chain widens the same value
# to 64 bytes (Q + '42' x 64), so a v3 enclave sets the wide form here. Read
# by a later workstream's wiring — the default keeps every existing path (the
# harness installs its fixture at the 20-byte address) exactly as it was.
# QRL_DEPOSIT_CONTRACT="0x4242424242424242424242424242424242424242"

# ---- testnet-profile deployment (scripts/lib/profile.js) ----
# The time-compressed build: one day is ten minutes, so an epoch is 70 minutes
# and the unbonding three and a half hours. The QRL leg stays on the enclave
# above; only the origin leg goes to a public testnet, and only under this
# profile. Keys are per chain, named after the manifest under ecdsa-stakings/.
#
# Hoodi is Ethereum's staking testnet (chain id 560048), where Lido's stETH is
# deployed. Holesky is gone.
HOODI_RPC_URL="https://<your hoodi rpc>"
HOODI_PRIVATE_KEY="<0x + 32 bytes>"
# or, equivalently, the phrase itself (first account of m/44'0'/60'/0'/0):
# HOODI_MNEMONIC="<12 or 24 words>"
# Written by `npm run deploy:evm -- --chain hoodi`; never reused across relays,
# because one seed behind two relays signs two root messages from one leaf.
# One seed per signer of the relay's set (whitepaper §3.6, D1): the manifest's
# rootSigners { threshold, signers } (one of one where absent). Each seed also
# grows that signer's three later generations of the authority chain. A host
# signs with the seeds it holds and needs k of them; HOODI_OTS_SEED is signer 0.
# HOODI_OTS_SEED_0=
# HOODI_OTS_SEED_1=
# HOODI_OTS_SEED_2=
# HOODI_OTS_SEED=
# HOODI_OTS_HEIGHT=

# The deployment the site reads (CLAUDE.md §4.3, "The permanent deployment").
# Its own manifest, its own relay, its own one-time seed, and its own Hoodi key:
# a deployment sent from the account a live relayer uses collides on the nonce.
HOODI_VPS_RPC_URL="https://<your hoodi rpc>"
HOODI_VPS_PRIVATE_KEY="<0x + 32 bytes>"   # gas only; funded by hand
# HOODI_VPS_OTS_SEED_0=    # written by deploy:evm -- --chain hoodi-vps (and _1, _2 for 2 of 3)
# HOODI_VPS_OTS_SEED=      # signer 0, as before
# HOODI_VPS_OTS_HEIGHT=

# A public origin RPC is refused without this. Separate from ALLOW_PUBLIC_RPC so
# that opening the origin chain never opens the QRL leg.
# ALLOW_PUBLIC_ORIGIN_RPC=1

# ---- origin chain (ECDSA / secp256k1) ----
# Private networks only, the same rule as QRL and for the same reason. The guard
# is a separate flag from ALLOW_PUBLIC_RPC on purpose: enabling a public origin
# RPC must never also enable a public QRL RPC, and the two chains fail
# differently — one leaves litter, the other spends real money.
ORIGIN_CHAIN=ethereum
ORIGIN_RPC_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8545"
ORIGIN_CHAIN_ID=1

# ---- relayer ----
# A secp256k1 key. It pays gas and nothing else: it never receives swept yield,
# because the escrow's sweep pays a destination fixed at construction.
RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY="<0x + 32 bytes>"
RELAYER_DRY_RUN=1
RELAYER_POLL_MS=12000
RELAYER_CONFIRMATIONS=12
RELAYER_DELIVERY_MARGIN_SECONDS=900
RELAYER_MAX_ATTEMPTS=6

# The QRL account holding ATTESTER_ROLE on AttestationVerifier. Distinct from
# DEPLOYER_MNEMONIC: sealing an epoch root and deploying are different powers.
ATTESTER_MNEMONIC="<34-word QRL mnemonic>"

# The beacon API of the enclave (qrysm serves /qrl/v1). kurtosis-up.sh writes it.
QRL_BEACON_URL="http://127.0.0.1:3500"

# ---- key separation on a shared network (audit 2026-09-27, D2/D3) ----
# On a manifest whose origin chain is real (hoodi, hoodi-vps: `client` evm),
# deployQrlLeg — deploy:testnet AND the relayer's --redeploy-qrl — refuses to
# run unless governance, the MockAttestation sealer and the deploying account
# (the relayer on the VPS) are three distinct accounts. Per-chain keys
# (HOODI_VPS_GOVERNANCE_ADDRESS, ...) win over the global ones. Local manifests
# (local, rehearsal) ignore all of this and use the deployer for every role.
#
# Governance of ArkStakeParams, ArkStakeRegistry and ArkBondDelegation. The
# deployment PROPOSES it; this account calls acceptGovernance() on each.
# GOVERNANCE_ADDRESS="<Q + 128 hex>"
# The MockAttestation sealer; the relayer seals roots from QRL_SEALER_MNEMONIC.
# SEALER_ADDRESS="<Q + 128 hex>"
# QRL_SEALER_MNEMONIC="<34-word QRL mnemonic, the SEALER_ADDRESS account>"
# The account that may move MockQDayOracle / MockPriceOracle. On a shared manifest
# it must not be the deployer (2026-09-28, item 78): REQUIRED for hoodi-vps.
# ORACLE_OPERATOR_ADDRESS="<Q + 128 hex>"
# Deploy on one key anyway, knowingly (logged as a WARNING). Leave unset.
# ALLOW_SHARED_KEYS=1
#
# The relayer reads MockQDayOracle into close/freeze leaves only on local
# manifests. On a shared one it logs the reading and queues nothing, unless:
# HOODI_VPS_QDAY_MOCK_ACTS=1
#
# The relayer inbox (`relay seal`). Every inbox file is an envelope signed with
# RELAYER_INBOX_KEY (secp256k1, NOT the one-time seed); the relayer ingests it
# only if the signer is allowlisted on ITS host. An empty allowlist refuses all.
# RELAYER_INBOX_KEY="<0x + 32 bytes, the operator's>"
# RELAYER_INBOX_SIGNERS="0x<operator address>[,0x<another>]"
# HOODI_VPS_INBOX_SIGNERS="0x<operator address>"

# ---- the QRL side after a devnet reset (2026-09-28, gap item 77) ----
# The relayer (`--redeploy-qrl`) redeploys the ecosystem layer's
# governance stack first — from vendor/core-governance/, where the manifest's
# `governance.selfDeploy` is true (hoodi-vps) — then funds the role accounts a
# fresh genesis does not fund, then the QRL leg wired to that stack. Core's
# names, the QRL network's (one stack per network, 2026-10-07); <CHAIN>_<NAME>
# (HOODI_VPS_GOV_PROPOSER_OWNERS, ...) is read only where <NAME> is absent. ADDRESSES
# only: no owner's or attester's key belongs on the VPS. Each must differ from
# the deployer (the relayer), SEALER_ADDRESS and ORACLE_OPERATOR_ADDRESS.
# GOV_PROPOSER_OWNERS="Q<128 hex>[,Q<128 hex>...]"   # S1 proposer multisig
# GOV_PROPOSER_THRESHOLD=1
# GOV_GUARDIAN_OWNERS="Q<128 hex>"                   # guardian multisig (cancel only)
# GOV_GUARDIAN_THRESHOLD=1
# Phase-1 TEST attesters of ArkQDayOracle: operator-held keys, five at least
# (the oracle's quorum), nine at most. Each is funded its bond + gas float.
# QDAY_ATTESTERS="Q<128 hex>,Q<128 hex>,Q<128 hex>,Q<128 hex>,Q<128 hex>"
# QDAY_ATTESTER_BOND=10000000000000000000000        # wei (10,000 QRL); uncalibrated
# QDAY_ADVISORY_COOLDOWN=4200                       # seconds; default seven profile days
# QDAY_COURT=                                       # who may slash attester bonds; default none
# GOV_PROPOSAL_THRESHOLD_BPS=10 GOV_QDAY_QUORUM_BPS=500 GOV_OBJECTION_THRESHOLD_BPS=2000
# GOV_ADMISSION_DEPOSIT=5000000000000000000000
# ARK_INCENTIVES= ARK_TREASURY= ARK_CONTRIBUTORS= ARK_BACKSTOP= ARK_LIQUIDITY=   # five distinct addresses; unset: incentives = deployer, treasury = timelock, the rest inert placeholders
# VEARK_PROTOCOL_OWNED=
# Gas float each role account is topped up to on a fresh genesis, in whole QRL.
# QRL_ROLE_FUNDING=100
# Where a record lives, where not the manifest's governance.record:
# GOVERNANCE_RECORD=deployments/governance-private-qrvm.json   # default: the manifest's governance.network
#
# On a shared manifest the price double's operator must not be the deployer
# either (item 38): ORACLE_OPERATOR_ADDRESS above is REQUIRED for hoodi-vps.
# The court: `real` (default; manifest `court`) or `mock`.
# ARK_COURT=real
#
# Build and vendor, once per change of core (see scripts/vendor-governance.js):
#   (ecosystem contracts) node scripts/compile.js --profile testnet
#   (ecosystem contracts) HYPC_DOCKER_IMAGE=hypc:local ARK_QRVM=1 node scripts/compile.js --profile testnet
#   npm run vendor:governance

# ---- the reference solver: the testnet's premium-swap market maker (2026-09-29) ----
# bin/solver.js, `ark-solver.service` on qrl-vps. Accounts of its OWN: on a
# shared manifest it refuses the deployer's, the sealer's, any role's and the
# relayer's origin key (exit 78), unless ALLOW_SHARED_KEYS=1. Its keys go to
# /etc/ark-staking/solver.env (read through ARK_ENV_FILE), never relayer.env.
# SOLVER_MNEMONIC="<34-word QRL mnemonic>"            # QRL; <CHAIN>_SOLVER_QRL_MNEMONIC wins
# SOLVER_ADDRESS="Q<128 hex>"                          # its address: the relayer's redeploy funds it; <CHAIN>_SOLVER_QRL_ADDRESS wins
# HOODI_VPS_SOLVER_PRIVATE_KEY="0x<32 bytes>"          # the origin chain (or HOODI_VPS_SOLVER_MNEMONIC); its ETH is a person's
# HOODI_VPS_SOLVER_ADDRESS="0x<20 bytes>"              # checked against the key
# QRL topped up at each fresh genesis, whole QRL (a day of lots, bonds, gas):
# SOLVER_QRL_FUNDING=25000
# Settings, <CHAIN>_SOLVER_<NAME> before SOLVER_<NAME>:
# SOLVER_SHARE_BPS=10000    # of what an offering may sell; raised to the D4 minimum lot
# SOLVER_PRICE_BPS=0        # above the reserve
# SOLVER_MAX_LOT_QRL=1000   # lot value cap, whole QRL
# SOLVER_QRL_RESERVE=50     # kept back for gas, whole QRL
# SOLVER_CLAIM_GAS=300000   # origin gas one claim needs; below it the solver warns and quotes nothing
# SOLVER_CARRY_AFTER=       # seconds after its own claim before it carries the preimage to QRL itself; default half the reveal budget
# SOLVER_INTERVAL=60
# Written by the installer into solver.env (derived from HOODI_VPS_PRIVATE_KEY here):
# HOODI_VPS_RELAYER_ADDRESS="0x<the relayer's Hoodi address>"
